If you've been following along and got confused at some point, then you've probably used the **log!** macro we wrote in [*Chapter 3*](B17151_03_Final_PG_ePub.xhtml#_idTextAnchor063), *Creating a Game Loop*, to see what was going on. If you have been doing that, congratulations! You've been debugging the same way I did when I wrote the code originally. Print line debugging is still standard in many languages and it's pretty much the only form of debugging that's guaranteed to work anywhere. If you haven't done that, then it looks like this:

